Toolkit. As you may know, ParaView's Python bindings cannot be installed with pip, leading to various headaches.\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:7:We provide instructions to install TopoPilot using Anaconda as well as Python virtual environments. The Anaconda version has no prerequisites (other than Anaconda) and is generally bette behaved. The Python virtual environment version requires that you already have ParaView and TTK installed on your machine, while the Anaconda version does not. It also will be more annoying to work with (see below)\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:18:```pip3 install -e TopoPilot2```\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:37:Finally, install TopoPilot by running\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:39:```pip3 install -e path/to/TopoPilot2```\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:78:```python3 -m pip install -e path/to/TopoPilot2```\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:90:TopoPilot supports the OpenAI and Anthropic APIs. Select an OpenAI or Claude\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:118:Set the standard provider environment variable before launching TopoPilot:\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:127:`openai_api_key.txt` or `anthropic_api_key.txt` next to `TopoPilot2Library`:\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:130:TopoPilot2/\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:133:└── TopoPilot2Library/\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:144:```TopoPilot```\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:146:To run just the viewer or just the server, you can instead run ```TopoPilot-Client``` or ```TopoPilot-Server```. If you are only using TopoPilot to perform and save computations, and do not need to visualize anything, then you only need to run the MCP server.\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/README.md:152:If that occurs, then instead of ```TopoPilot```, run ```TopoPilot-NoBatch```, and instead of ```TopoPilot-Client``` run ```TopoPilot-Client-NoBatch```.\n/workspace/TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/types/pointTrackingTy